{
  "dom_id": "step-615764",
  "name": "Example: \n                    Expressing Subsequent Percentages as a Single Percentage",
  "problem": "According to a recent report, $40\\%$ of viewers said they enjoyed documentaries. Of those, $50\\%$ preferred documentaries about nature. What percentage of all viewers preferred nature documentaries?",
  "worked_solution": "Let $x$ be the total number of viewers.\n\nWe're told that $40\\%$ of viewers enjoyed documentaries. Thus, the number of viewers who enjoy documentaries is \n\n$$\n0.4x.\n$$\n\nWe are also told that of those viewers who enjoy documentaries, $50\\%$ preferred nature topics. So, the number of viewers who preferred nature documentaries is\n\n$$\n0.50(0.4x) = 0.20x.\n$$\n\nThe expression $0.20x$ represents $20\\%$ of $x.$ Therefore, $20\\%$ of all viewers preferred nature documentaries.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
